meta {
  name: Update - status push (Scheduled to Active)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{empBaseUrl}}/updateFeatures
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  f: json
  token: {{empApiKey}}
  rollbackOnFailure: true
  features: [{"attributes":{"OBJECTID":1000,"Status":"Active"}}]
}

docs {
  What the nightly job's status push sends - this is the new behaviour ML-1500
  adds. Note how little it carries: only the OBJECTID and the new Status. The
  push deliberately does not resend the whole feature.

  Swap Status for "Expired" or "Withdrawn" to exercise the other transitions.
  Withdrawn is sent by the existing withdrawal path, unchanged by this ticket.

  Expect: 200, updateResults echoing OBJECTID 1000 back rather than allocating
  a new id - otherwise the backend's stored feature ids would drift on every
  update.
}
